laurel (Mi A3, iOS 26): rasterization order only for a shader that really reads an attachment. metal2vulkan asks it of every pipeline of a device with rasterization-order access, because a pass cannot foresee which of its draws fetch: GMEM drew with FLUSH_PER_OVERLAP on every draw, and sysmem was never chosen. Now a writer needs no flush; a reader after a writer gets a barrier at its draw. Kill switch NEGRONIMETAL_READERS=0. Docs: docs/laurel_sprout/ios26-default-speed.md.

diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc
index 2474ad8..c34cac9 100644
